NOTICE — vendored and fetched data

This repository builds on public linguistic resources. The code is
MIT-licensed (see LICENSE); the data below carries its own terms, and
every fetched artifact is pinned by checksum in the manifests under
mirror/data/fixtures/.

- CMU Pronouncing Dictionary (via the Elfix preprocessed lexicon):
  Carnegie Mellon University, BSD-style license (free use with
  attribution; see the cmudict distribution for the exact text).
- UniMorph English (unimorph/eng): CC BY-SA 3.0. Kirov et al. 2018;
  Batsuren et al. 2022. Fetched by mirror/scripts/fetch_unimorph.py;
  not redistributed here beyond the checksummed manifest.
- BLiMP (alexwarstadt/blimp): benchmark paradigms, used for
  evaluation; the 34 agreement-family paradigms are vendored under
  mirror/tests/fixtures/blimp/ for reproducible tests, the rest
  fetched by mirror/scripts/fetch_blimp.py.
- WordSim-353 (Finkelstein et al. 2001; sim/rel split Agirre et al.
  2009) and SimLex-999 (Hill et al. 2015), via
  vecto-ai/word-benchmarks: vendored under
  mirror/tests/fixtures/meaning/ for the sentinel tests.
- Project Gutenberg texts (the corpus_10m book list and the NLTK
  Gutenberg selection): public domain in the United States; the full
  source list with IDs is in
  mirror/data/fixtures/corpus_10m_manifest.json. Fetched by
  mirror/scripts/fetch_corpus_10m.py; not redistributed.
- NLTK Brown and Reuters corpora: distributed by NLTK under their
  respective licenses; used to build the pinned running-text corpora.

The pinned corpus files that ship in this repository
(mirror/data/corpus.txt, mirror/data/corpus_big.txt) are normalized
running-text derivatives of the sources above under the Elfix data
contract, carried as research artifacts with their provenance
recorded in mirror/data/README.md and the HANDOFF.
